Consider a senior economist studying the impact of monetary policy changes on inflation and unemployment rates. The economist uses a time-series dataset comprising quarterly observations of interest rates, inflation, and unemployment rates over 20 years.

1. The economist decides to apply a Vector Autoregression (VAR) model to understand the dynamic relationship between these variables. Suppose the VAR model includes three endogenous variables: interest rates (IR), inflation (INF), and unemployment rate (UR). The VAR(1) model can be represented as:

   \[
   \begin{bmatrix}
   IR_t \\
   INF_t \\
   UR_t
   \end{bmatrix}
   = 
   \begin{bmatrix}
   a_1 \\
   a_2 \\
   a_3
   \end{bmatrix}
   + 
   \begin{bmatrix}
   b_{11} & b_{12} & b_{13} \\
   b_{21} & b_{22} & b_{23} \\
   b_{31} & b_{32} & b_{33}
   \end{bmatrix}
   \begin{bmatrix}
   IR_{t-1} \\
   INF_{t-1} \\
   UR_{t-1}
   \end{bmatrix}
   +
   \begin{bmatrix}
   \epsilon_{1t} \\
   \epsilon_{2t} \\
   \epsilon_{3t}
   \end{bmatrix}
   \]

   Given that the economist has estimated the parameters, determine the stability condition of the VAR(1) model in terms of its characteristic roots.

